Title: Aunt Hannah
Order: 21
Production Code: 1x21

EXT. WOODS NEAR LIVINGSTON HALL - DAY

AMB: wind, dry leaves

[[Dianthe Lusk]] wanders, lost, until a cabin appears in a clearing and an old woman steps out as if she'd been expected.

AUNT HANNAH
Come in, honey, and res'.

INT. AUNT HANNAH'S CABIN - CONTINUOUS

AMB: a hearth fire

Warmed by coffee, Dianthe asks the old woman's name — and gets, instead, a question back.

AUNT HANNAH
Hain't it these arms done nussed ev'ry Livingston? I knowed your mother, child. For all you're married to Marse Aubrey, you isn't a white 'ooman.

DIANTHE LUSK
(quietly)
I don't deny it.

With a cry, [[Hannah]] pulls her close.

AUNT HANNAH
Gawd-a-mercy — my Mira's gal!

She tells it all: taken to the big house as a tot, her relations with old massa; Mira, the only one of ten children he left her. Then young marse, the elder Dr. Livingston, took a shine to Mira. Reuel was Mira's first. Dianthe, her second.

AUNT HANNAH (CONT'D)
Den de Doctor married a white lady, an' when she found out de family secrets she made de house too hot to hol' Mira, an' she mus' be sold. A week before, Misses' child was born an' died in about an hour — 'bout de same time Mira had a son, too. In de 'citemen' I changed de babies, honey. Tol' Marse Livingston dat Mira's boy was de dead one. So Aubrey is your own blood brother.

DIANTHE LUSK
(reeling)
My brothers. Both of them.

Hannah bares her own chest — a lotus-lily mark, the same as Dianthe's own.

AUNT HANNAH
All of Mira's children bear it. All of one blood.

Dianthe faints into the old woman's arms.
